  "rebuildInstructions": [
    "Use native MSYS2 CLANG64 for amd64 or CLANGARM64 for arm64. Retain the package versions above and the complete licenses/windows-toolchain notices.",
    "The original, unmodified source archives are in sources/windows. The complete MinGW tree conservatively covers headers and runtime, including potentially LGPL portions.",
    "In a separate build workspace unpack the MSYS2 recipe snapshot; use mingw-w64-libiconv/PKGBUILD with the included libiconv-1.19.1.tar.gz, both patches and iconv.pc. Run makepkg-mingw --syncdeps --cleanbuild in the matching shell. PKGBUILD prepare/build/package functions are authoritative, including generated files and configure flags.",
    "MinGW headers/CRT/winpthreads use the fixed full MinGW source archive and the matching recipe directories. LLVM runtime rebuilding uses mingw-w64-llvm/PKGBUILD and its fixed upstream sources/patches; its Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception LICENSE files and historical notices accompany the binaries. The snapshot is a recipe, not a bundled LLVM upstream source archive.",
    "Rebuild libmpv and project libraries with the bundled common fixed-source recipe. Capture the final LLD map and inputs after linking and rerun this runtime review. Link evidence records actual archive/object hashes and package provenance, not a claim that static or LGPL code is absent."
  ]
